 The receipt's form rule is: key starting code:/mouse/switch: -> that form; key == "" AND keycode != 0 -> code; otherwise named. The 42 code binds are the same fact step 2 and step 3 describe: Hyprland stores a `code:N` bind with an **empty key field plus a keycode**, so no `key` field ever carries the literal `code:` prefix and the form must be recovered from the keycode. Those 42 sit on 14 distinct keycodes (`10-21`, `61`, `201`). A second read-only capture of the same JSON (receipt `.ufo/waves/round-49/receipts/binds-shape-r49.txt`, 1005 B) gives the per-field shape and the modifier-mask histogram:
